ENTRY 9425 {"id":9425,"kind":"pi.user","messages":[{"role":"user","text":"Area: sandbox lifecycle in the orchestrator. Files: packages/orchestrator/src/{sandboxes.ts,lifecycle.ts,sweep.ts,sweeper.ts,kube.ts} and docs/decisions/0002-0004. Questions: can the orphan sweep delete a live session's claim or PVC (races with creation, empty or failed session queries, name/label edge cases)? Can suspend/resume or the pod recycle-on-interrupt race with an in-flight tool call? Are timers and bridge processes leaked? Is the per-claim token check on adoption correct?\n\nYou are doing a focused bug hunt on the repository cloned at /workspace/repo (pi-durable-k8s: durable Pi agents on Kubernetes; read /workspace/repo/README.md first for orientation).\n\nRules:\n- Static review only. Node is not installed in this sandbox, so you cannot run the tests; use bash, grep, sed, find and git to read code.\n- Look for real defects: wrong behaviour, races, crash/restart bugs, security holes, resource leaks, broken error handling. No style or naming nits, no \"consider adding tests\".\n- For every finding, re-read the code to confirm it before reporting. Prefer 3 solid findings over 8 guesses.\n- Do not modify anything outside /workspace, do not push, do not open network connections other than what git already did.\n- Stay within about 40 tool calls.\n\nFinish with a report in exactly this format (Markdown), and end it with the line END-OF-REPORT:\n\n## Findings\n### <n>. <one-line title>\n- Severity: high | medium | low\n- Confidence: high | medium | low\n- Location: <path>:<line>\n- What happens: <concrete failure scenario: inputs/state -> wrong result>\n- Evidence: <short quote of the relevant code>\n- Fix idea: <one or two sentences>\n\n## Areas checked with no findings\n<bullets>\n\nEND-OF-REPORT"}]}
ENTRY 9433 {"id":9433,"kind":"pi.assistant","messages":[{"role":"assistant","text":"","calls":["bash({\"command\":\"cat README.md\"})"]}]}
